  "query_preview": "..For much of this week southeast Arizona will be \nin a favorable monsoon flow pattern that will keep daily chances\nof showers and thunderstorms in the forecast for much of the \narea with day-to-day variability in coverage of storms. There \nwill be the continued daily hazards of severe wind gusts, blowing\ndust and flash flooding. WPC has highlighted Monday and Tuesday\nfor enhanced chances for increased flash flooding threat. Not \neveryone will get rain every day this week which is the monsoon\nin a nutshell. High temperatures today will remain hot then be\naround normal for the work week.\n\nFor today, drier air that has pushed into the eastern zones will\nlimit thunderstorms, especially across Cochise county. The main\narea for concern later this afternoon into early this evening\nwill be west of Sells, where CAMs are indicating a few strong to\nsevere storms are possible along with heavy rain as dewpoints\nare in the low 60s and PWATs around 1.5\". 09/00z HREF has \nneighborhood probabilities of 10-30% for 50+ knots. Added patchy\ndust to the forecast for the western areas.",
